// Title: Import LDAP Data Interchange Format File Via Ldifde.EXE
// Sigma ID: 6f535e01-ca1f-40be-ab8d-45b19c0c8b7f
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: @gott_cyber
// Date: 2022-09-02 | Modified: 2023-03-14
// ATT&CK: command-and-control, stealth, T1218, T1105
// Description: Detects the execution of "Ldifde.exe" with the import flag "-i". The can be abused to include
//   HTTP-based arguments which will allow the arbitrary download of files from a remote server.
// False positives:
//   - Since the content of the files are unknown, false positives are expected
// References:
//   - https://twitter.com/0gtweet/status/1564968845726580736
//   - https://strontic.github.io/xcyclopedia/library/ldifde.exe-979DE101F5059CEC1D2C56967CA2BAC0.html
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/previous-versions/windows/it-pro/windows-server-2012-r2-and-2012/cc731033(v=ws.11)
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_ldifde_file_load.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\ldifde.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "ldifde.exe") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "-i" and ProcessCommandLine contains "-f")
